Fold long lines in the crash-report dumper + sweetdumptreename filter.

The 0134 dumper works (it listed /private/var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter
and dumped SpringBoard .ips files), but it printed every source line as `CF| `
plus at most 200 characters and DROPPED the rest.  The .ips report is JSON
with very long single lines (`lastExceptionBacktrace` ~2.8 KB, `threads`
longer), so the exception backtrace was cut after two frames.

0136 (bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c only):
  - fold every source line into chunks of <=180 characters, nothing dropped:
        CF| <chunk>       first chunk of a source line
        CF+| <chunk>      continuation of the previous source line
    Reassemble by concatenating the payloads in order (CF| starts a new line,
    CF+| continues the current one).
  - `sweetdumptreename=<substr>` (default empty = all): only dump the content
    of files whose name contains the substring, e.g. SpringBoard; the TREE
    listing still shows every entry.
  - default `sweetdumptreemax` raised to 1 MiB (1048576), still overridable
    with the same boot arg.
  - 4 KiB bounded reads / read-only vnode operations unchanged.

Next dump-cycle boot args:
  sweetdumptree=/private/var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter
  sweetdumptreename=SpringBoard
  sweetdumptreetime=90
  sweetdumptreemax=1048576
  sweetrebootat=600
Expected console (-> SWEETLOG -> TWRP pull):
  TREE: thread start
  TREE: 1 dirs, ext=ips, name=SpringBoard, wait=90 s, max=1048576
  TREE /private/var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter entry=SpringBoard-....ips type=1 size=50612
  CRASHFILE /private/.../SpringBoard-....ips size=50612
  CF| {"app_name":"SpringBoard",...
  CF+| ...long JSON continues here...
  CRASHFILE end /private/.../SpringBoard-....ips
  TREE: end printed=...
  (then SWEET REBOOT / WDT reset)
